Runtime dependencies (not bundled — installed separately)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No dependency licence conflicts with this Apache-2.0 release. Dependencies are
installed from their own distributions rather than vendored here, so their terms
travel with them, not with this source. `docs/licensing.md` carries the
per-package audit — including the weak-copyleft packages (MPL-2.0) and the
binaries described next, neither of which constrains this release.

**Copyleft reaches this project as binaries, not as source.** Three places, and
all three matter only to someone REDISTRIBUTING a build rather than using the
source:

- **The Docker images** built from this repository bundle a GPL-licensed ffmpeg
  from the base distribution.
- **The `av` (PyAV) wheel**, a dependency of faster-whisper and therefore
  present in every install, bundles an LGPL-v3 FFmpeg build together with
  `libx264` and `libx265`, which are GPL-2.0-or-later.
- **The `opencv-python-headless` wheel** (the `track` extra) bundles its own
  LGPL ffmpeg.

qatf itself invokes ffmpeg as a SUBPROCESS and never links against it, so none
of this extends to this source. If you redistribute an image or a bundle that
CONTAINS these binaries, comply with their terms for the build you shipped.

Whisper model weights are downloaded at runtime by faster-whisper and are not
part of this repository.
